# Keep the build context small and stop local secrets reaching the daemon.
#
# .env.local MUST be excluded. PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL is passed as a build ARG and
# every other env var lives on the Convex deployment, but shipping a developer's
# local .env into an image is the kind of mistake that is only discovered later.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
build
.svelte-kit
dist

# Convex FUNCTION source is not part of the web image - it is deployed separately
# with `npx convex deploy`. Sending it would only bloat the context.
#
# BUT src/convex/_generated MUST come along, or the image cannot build.
#
# This exclusion used to be the whole `src/convex` directory, which shipped an image
# whose production build failed on missing modules: nine web modules import the
# generated `api` proxy at runtime (src/lib/convex/client.svelte.ts and every route
# that calls a Convex function), and the generated directory sits inside the one
# that was excluded. Nobody had caught it because nothing here has ever run
# `docker build`.
#
# Files are excluded rather than the directory ON PURPOSE. Docker stops descending
# into an excluded directory, so a `!src/convex/_generated` exception placed after
# `src/convex` would never be evaluated - the exclusion has to leave the directory
# itself in the walk.
src/convex/*.ts
src/convex/*.js
!src/convex/_generated
convex.json
scripts

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

*.log
npm-debug.log*
